    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Let me summarize the full-stack change I made for the invoice lifecycle (DRAFT \u2192 SENT \u2192 PAID).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request asked for invoices to move through stages \u2014 draft, sent, paid \u2014 with a record kept when sent, and payment only allowed after sending. Here's what I implemented across the stack:\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V8__invoices_draft_default.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration changing the `status` column default from `UNPAID` to `DRAFT`, so new invoices begin in the draft stage.\n\n**Server**\n- `invoice/SendInvoice.java` + `officefloor/rest/api/invoices/{id}/send.POST.yml` \u2014 new endpoint that flips a `DRAFT` invoice to `SENT`, guards that only a draft can be sent, and records the audit line `INVOICE_SENT id=<id> amount=<amount>` via the `Audit` service.\n- `invoice/PayInvoice.java` \u2014 now rejects payment (409) unless the invoice is `SENT`, enforcing \"only pay once sent.\"\n- `invoice/CreateInvoice.java` \u2014 new invoices now start as `DRAFT` instead of `UNPAID`.\n- `TestSupportController.java` (seed path, non-pinned app code) \u2014 the invoice seed now omits the optional date columns when a fixture doesn't supply them, so the table defaults apply instead of inserting `null` into NOT NULL columns; status defaults to `DRAFT`. This was needed because the new spec seeds invoices without dates.\n\n**Front-end** (`features/projects/feature.tsx`)\n- Added a `invoice-send-<id>` button shown only when the invoice is `DRAFT` (calls the send endpoint).\n- The existing `invoice-pay-<id>` button now shows only when status is `SENT` (previously any non-PAID), so a draft can't be paid.\n\nThe change is additive and local: a new migration, a new endpoint (YAML + logic class), and composition within the existing projects feature. No `data-testid` was renamed or removed. `bin/e2e` passes both acceptance tests.",
